# 17. Duplicate Detection

Duplicate detection will use a simple, explainable scoring system.

## 17.1 Signals

### Location

Calculate distance between the new report and recent incidents.

Default:

```text
Urban radius: 300 meters
Time window: 10 minutes
```

### Text

Compare normalized keywords.

Example:

```text
Report A:
"Fire at central market near gate 2"

Report B:
"Large fire near central market gate"
```

High similarity → duplicate candidate.

## 17.2 Duplicate Score

```text
Location match       = 40%
Time match           = 20%
Text similarity      = 40%

Duplicate score =
locationScore +
timeScore +
textScore
```

If:

```text
score >= 0.75
```

show:

> Possible duplicate incident

Do NOT automatically merge in the first MVP.

The operator should click:

```text
Merge Reports
```

