# 55. Complete Demo Scenario

## Scenario: Market Fire

### Step 1 — Citizen A

Reports:

> "There is a large fire near the market and people are trapped."

### Step 2 — Citizen B

Reports:

> "Smoke and fire visible near the same market."

### Step 3 — System

The backend:

```text
receives reports
      ↓
classifies as FIRE
      ↓
estimates CRITICAL
      ↓
assigns P1
      ↓
checks recent nearby incidents
      ↓
detects possible duplicate
```

### Step 4 — Operator

Dashboard displays:

```text
Possible duplicate detected

Existing Incident:
INC-10024

New Report:
REP-10031

[Merge]
[Keep Separate]
```

Operator chooses:

```text
Merge
```

### Step 5 — AI Summary

System generates:

> Large fire reported near a crowded market with multiple corroborating reports. Immediate fire response and medical support are recommended.

### Step 6 — Resource Engine

Recommended:

```text
Fire Team FT-04
Ambulance AMB-02
Police Unit PU-03
```

### Step 7 — Operator

Clicks:

```text
Dispatch
```

### Step 8 — Real-Time Update

Responder screen receives:

```text
NEW ASSIGNMENT
INC-10024
Market Fire
Priority: P1
```

### Step 9 — Responder

Changes:

```text
Assigned
→ En Route
→ On Scene
```

Dashboard updates instantly.

### Step 10 — Escalation

If the operator intentionally delays the demo:

```text
P1 response SLA exceeded
```

Dashboard displays:

```text
CRITICAL ESCALATION
```

### Step 11 — Resolution

Responder clicks:

```text
Resolve Incident
```

### Step 12 — Analytics

The system records:

```text
Response time
Resource usage
Incident duration
Incident type
Final status
```

The analytics dashboard updates.

